---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Install" description="Install the daily Rust command-line tools with Cargo." current="install">
  <section class="shell page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Install</p>
    <h1>Install the command.</h1>
    <p>Build the executable with Cargo and use its subcommands from your terminal.</p>
  </section>
  <article class="shell article">
    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul><li>Rust and Cargo</li><li>Node.js is only needed to work on this website</li></ul>
    <h2>Download a prebuilt release</h2>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/cotanjant/daily/releases/latest">Get the latest release</a> for Linux, macOS, or Windows. On Linux and macOS, mark the downloaded binary as executable with <code>chmod +x daily-*</code>, then move it to a directory on your <code>PATH</code>.</p>
    <h2>Install from this checkout</h2>
    <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/cotanjant/daily.git
cd daily
cargo install --path .</code></pre>
    <h2>Run without installing</h2>
    <pre><code>cargo run -- --help
cargo run -- download https://example.com/file.zip file.zip</code></pre>
    <p>See the <a href="https://github.com/cotanjant/daily/blob/main/docs/usage.md">command guide</a> for examples.</p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
